  "overview": {
    "title": "Blue boats and daily catch",
    "p1": "El Jadida’s fishing port is still a place of work: painted blue boats, nets drying, and the rhythm of boats leaving and returning. It is one of the most photogenic and honest corners of the town.",
    "p2": "Come in the morning for activity. Stay out of restricted dock zones and ask before close-up photos of people at work. Grilled fish nearby is the natural follow-up.",
    "p3": "The port sits close to the old town, so it fits easily between the cistern circuit and a medina afternoon."
